§§ `Part 2 -- Requirements for recognition of a professional qualification`

-- ---- paragraph 6: Entry requirements ----

-- src:20472 | (2) In relation to a person who has not been admitted to a university or other similar establishment in the United Kingdom, “attaining university entrance level” means—
-- src:20473 | (a) being educated to such a standard as would entitle him to be considered for such admission on the basis of—
-- src:20474 | (i) academic or professional qualifications obtained in the United Kingdom and recognised by the Secretary of State to be of an appropriate standard, or
-- src:20475 | (ii) academic or professional qualifications obtained outside the United Kingdom which the Secretary of State considers to be of an equivalent standard, or
-- src:20476 | (b) being assessed, on the basis of written tests of a kind appearing to the Secretary of State to be adequate for the purpose (with or without oral examination), as of such a standard of ability as would entitle him to be considered for such admission.
@ref sch 11 para 6(2) "attaining university entrance level" (src:20472-20476)
GIVEN `the person has been admitted to a university or other similar establishment in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is educated to such a standard as would entitle them to be considered for such admission on the basis of academic or professional qualifications obtained in the United Kingdom and recognised by the Secretary of State to be of an appropriate standard` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is educated to such a standard as would entitle them to be considered for such admission on the basis of academic or professional qualifications obtained outside the United Kingdom which the Secretary of State considers to be of an equivalent standard` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has been assessed on the basis of written tests of a kind appearing to the Secretary of State to be adequate for the purpose as of such a standard of ability as would entitle them to be considered for such admission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 11 para 6(2) the person has attained university entrance level` MEANS
    IF `the person has been admitted to a university or other similar establishment in the United Kingdom`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In relation to a person who has not been admitted to a university or other similar establishment in the United Kingdom"
    ELSE IF    `the person is educated to such a standard as would entitle them to be considered for such admission on the basis of academic or professional qualifications obtained in the United Kingdom and recognised by the Secretary of State to be of an appropriate standard`
            OR `the person is educated to such a standard as would entitle them to be considered for such admission on the basis of academic or professional qualifications obtained outside the United Kingdom which the Secretary of State considers to be of an equivalent standard`
            OR `the person has been assessed on the basis of written tests of a kind appearing to the Secretary of State to be adequate for the purpose as of such a standard of ability as would entitle them to be considered for such admission`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“attaining university entrance level” means"

-- src:20477 | (3) The assessment, tests and oral examination referred to in sub-paragraph (2)(b) may be conducted by—
-- src:20478 | (a) the qualifying body, or
-- src:20479 | (b) some other body approved by the Secretary of State.
@ref sch 11 para 6(3) Who may conduct the assessment, tests and oral examination (src:20477-20479)
GIVEN `the assessment is conducted by the qualifying body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assessment is conducted by some other body approved by the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 11 para 6(3) the assessment may be conducted by the body` MEANS
    IF `the assessment is conducted by the qualifying body` OR `the assessment is conducted by some other body approved by the Secretary of State`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may be conducted by"

-- src:20480 | (4) The reference in sub-paragraph (1)(b) to “a sufficient period of professional experience” is to not less than seven years' experience in a professional capacity in the fields of finance, law and accountancy.
@ref sch 11 para 6(4) "a sufficient period of professional experience" (src:20480-20480)
GIVEN `the years of experience in a professional capacity in the fields of finance, law and accountancy` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 11 para 6(4) the person has a sufficient period of professional experience` MEANS
    IF `the years of experience in a professional capacity in the fields of finance, law and accountancy` AT LEAST 7
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is to not less than seven years' experience"

-- src:20469 | 6 (1) The qualification must only be open to persons who—
-- src:20470 | (a) have attained university entrance level, or
-- src:20471 | (b) have a sufficient period of professional experience.
@ref sch 11 para 6(1) The qualification must only be open to persons with university entrance level or sufficient professional experience (src:20469-20471)
GIVEN `the person has attained university entrance level` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the person has a sufficient period of professional experience` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 11 para 6(1) the qualification may be open to the person` MEANS
    IF (`the person has attained university entrance level` EQUALS JUST TRUE) OR (`the person has a sufficient period of professional experience` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF (`the person has attained university entrance level` EQUALS JUST FALSE) AND (`the person has a sufficient period of professional experience` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must only be open to persons who"
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): university entrance level for a person already admitted, or an unknown fact

-- ---- paragraph 7: Requirement for theoretical instruction or professional experience ----

-- src:20482 | 7 (1) The qualification must be restricted to persons who—
-- src:20483 | (a) have completed a course of theoretical instruction in the subjects prescribed for the purposes of paragraph 8, or
-- src:20484 | (b) have a sufficient period of professional experience.
-- src:20485 | (2) The reference in sub-paragraph (1)(b) to “a sufficient period of professional experience” is to not less than seven years' experience in a professional capacity in the fields of finance, law and accountancy.
@ref sch 11 para 7 The qualification must be restricted to persons who completed a course of theoretical instruction or have professional experience (src:20482-20485)
GIVEN `the person has completed a course of theoretical instruction in the subjects prescribed for the purposes of paragraph 8` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the years of experience in a professional capacity in the fields of finance, law and accountancy` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 11 para 7 the qualification may be restricted to the person` MEANS
    IF `the person has completed a course of theoretical instruction in the subjects prescribed for the purposes of paragraph 8`
       OR `the years of experience in a professional capacity in the fields of finance, law and accountancy` AT LEAST 7
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be restricted to persons who"

-- ---- paragraph 8: Examination ----

-- src:20487 | 8 (1) The qualification must be restricted to persons who have passed an examination (at least part of which is in writing) testing—
-- src:20488 | (a) theoretical knowledge of the subjects prescribed for the purposes of this paragraph by regulations made by the Secretary of State, and
-- src:20489 | (b) ability to apply that knowledge in practice,
-- src:20490 | and requiring a standard of attainment at least equivalent to that required to obtain a degree from a university or similar establishment in the United Kingdom.
@ref sch 11 para 8(1) The qualification must be restricted to persons who have passed an examination of the kind described (src:20487-20490)
GIVEN `the examination is at least in part in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the examination tests theoretical knowledge of the subjects prescribed for the purposes of this paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the examination tests ability to apply that knowledge in practice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the examination requires a standard of attainment at least equivalent to that required to obtain a degree from a university or similar establishment in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 11 para 8(1) the examination is of the kind the qualification must require` MEANS
    IF    `the examination is at least in part in writing`
       AND `the examination tests theoretical knowledge of the subjects prescribed for the purposes of this paragraph`
       AND `the examination tests ability to apply that knowledge in practice`
       AND `the examination requires a standard of attainment at least equivalent to that required to obtain a degree from a university or similar establishment in the United Kingdom`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be restricted to persons who have passed an examination"

-- src:20491 | (2) The qualification may be awarded to a person without his theoretical knowledge of a subject being tested by examination if he has passed a university or other examination of equivalent standard in that subject or holds a university degree or equivalent qualification in it.
@ref sch 11 para 8(2) Theoretical knowledge of a subject need not be tested if already shown (src:20491-20491)
GIVEN `the person has passed a university or other examination of equivalent standard in that subject` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person holds a university degree or equivalent qualification in that subject` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 11 para 8(2) the qualification may be awarded without the theoretical knowledge of the subject being tested by examination` MEANS
    IF `the person has passed a university or other examination of equivalent standard in that subject` OR `the person holds a university degree or equivalent qualification in that subject`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if he has passed a university or other examination of equivalent standard in that subject or holds a university degree or equivalent qualification in it"

-- src:20492 | (3) The qualification may be awarded to a person without his ability to apply his theoretical knowledge of a subject in practice being tested by examination if he has received practical training in that subject which is attested by an examination or diploma recognised by the Secretary of State for the purposes of this paragraph.
@ref sch 11 para 8(3) Ability to apply knowledge in practice need not be tested if practical training is attested (src:20492-20492)
GIVEN `the person has received practical training in that subject which is attested by an examination or diploma recognised by the Secretary of State for the purposes of this paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 11 para 8(3) the qualification may be awarded without the ability to apply the theoretical knowledge of the subject in practice being tested by examination` MEANS
    IF `the person has received practical training in that subject which is attested by an examination or diploma recognised by the Secretary of State for the purposes of this paragraph`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if he has received practical training in that subject which is attested by an examination or diploma"

-- ---- paragraph 9: Practical training ----

-- src:20495 | 9 (1) The qualification must be restricted to persons who have completed at least three years' practical training of which—
-- src:20496 | (a) part was spent being trained in statutory audit work, and
-- src:20497 | (b) a substantial part was spent being trained in statutory audit work or other audit work of a description approved by the Secretary of State as being similar to statutory audit work.
@ref sch 11 para 9(1) The qualification must be restricted to persons who have completed at least three years' practical training (src:20495-20497)
GIVEN `the months of practical training the person has completed` IS A NUMBER
      `part of the training was spent being trained in statutory audit work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a substantial part of the training was spent being trained in statutory audit work or other audit work of a description approved by the Secretary of State as being similar to statutory audit work` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 11 para 9(1) the practical training meets the requirement` MEANS
    IF    `the months of practical training the person has completed` AT LEAST 36
       AND `part of the training was spent being trained in statutory audit work`
       AND `a substantial part of the training was spent being trained in statutory audit work or other audit work of a description approved by the Secretary of State as being similar to statutory audit work`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be restricted to persons who have completed at least three years' practical training"

-- src:20498 | (2) For the purpose of sub-paragraph (1) “statutory audit work” includes the work of a person appointed as the auditor of a person under the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom where it appears to the Secretary of State that the law and practice with respect to the audit of accounts is similar to that in the United Kingdom.
@ref sch 11 para 9(2) "statutory audit work" includes work as an auditor outside the United Kingdom where the law and practice are similar (src:20498-20498)
GIVEN `the work is the work of a statutory auditor` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the work is that of a person appointed as the auditor of a person under the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it appears to the Secretary of State that the law and practice with respect to the audit of accounts in that country or territory are similar to those in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 11 para 9(2) the work is statutory audit work` MEANS
    IF `the work is the work of a statutory auditor`
       OR (`the work is that of a person appointed as the auditor of a person under the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom` AND `it appears to the Secretary of State that the law and practice with respect to the audit of accounts in that country or territory are similar to those in the United Kingdom`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "“statutory audit work” includes"

-- src:20499 | (3) The training must be given by persons approved by the body offering the qualification as persons whom the body is satisfied, in the light of undertakings given by them and the supervision to which they are subject (whether by the body itself or some other body or organisation), will provide adequate training.
@ref sch 11 para 9(3) The training must be given by persons approved by the body (src:20499-20499)
GIVEN `the training is given by persons approved by the body offering the qualification as persons whom the body is satisfied, in the light of undertakings given by them and the supervision to which they are subject, will provide adequate training` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 11 para 9(3) the training is given as required` MEANS
    IF `the training is given by persons approved by the body offering the qualification as persons whom the body is satisfied, in the light of undertakings given by them and the supervision to which they are subject, will provide adequate training`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The training must be given by persons approved by the body"

-- src:20503 | (4A) Those conditions are that—
-- src:20504 | (a) the Secretary of State has determined for the purposes of sub-paragraph (2) that the law and practice with respect to the audit of accounts in the country or territory outside the United Kingdom is similar to that in the United Kingdom,
-- src:20505 | (b) the body offering the qualification is satisfied that the person has been approved by the body or organisation responsible for approving a person as being eligible under the law of the country or territory outside of the United Kingdom for appointment as an auditor of accounts, and
-- src:20506 | (c) the body offering the qualification is satisfied that the approval corresponds to the approval of a person as being eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor in the United Kingdom.
@ref sch 11 para 9(4A) The conditions for a corresponding appointment outside the United Kingdom (src:20503-20506)
GIVEN `the Secretary of State has determined for the purposes of sub-paragraph (2) that the law and practice with respect to the audit of accounts in the country or territory outside the United Kingdom is similar to that in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body offering the qualification is satisfied that the person has been approved by the body or organisation responsible for approving a person as being eligible under the law of that country or territory for appointment as an auditor of accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body offering the qualification is satisfied that the approval corresponds to the approval of a person as being eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor in the United Kingdom` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 11 para 9(4A) the conditions are met in relation to the person` MEANS
    IF    `the Secretary of State has determined for the purposes of sub-paragraph (2) that the law and practice with respect to the audit of accounts in the country or territory outside the United Kingdom is similar to that in the United Kingdom`
       AND `the body offering the qualification is satisfied that the person has been approved by the body or organisation responsible for approving a person as being eligible under the law of that country or territory for appointment as an auditor of accounts`
       AND `the body offering the qualification is satisfied that the approval corresponds to the approval of a person as being eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor in the United Kingdom`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Those conditions are that"

-- src:20500 | (4) At least two-thirds of the training must be given by a person—
-- src:20501 | (a) eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor, or
-- src:20502 | (b) eligible for a corresponding appointment as an auditor under the law of a country or territory outside the United Kingdom, where the conditions in sub-paragraph (4A) are met in relation to that person. ....
@ref sch 11 para 9(4) At least two-thirds of the training must be given by an eligible person (src:20500-20502)
GIVEN `the months of training given by a person eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` IS A NUMBER
      `the months of training given by a person eligible for a corresponding appointment outside the United Kingdom for whom the conditions in sub-paragraph (4A) are met` IS A NUMBER
      `the total months of training` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 11 para 9(4) at least two-thirds of the training is given by a person of the kind required` MEANS
    IF (`the months of training given by a person eligible for appointment as a statutory auditor` PLUS `the months of training given by a person eligible for a corresponding appointment outside the United Kingdom for whom the conditions in sub-paragraph (4A) are met`) TIMES 3 AT LEAST `the total months of training` TIMES 2
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "At least two-thirds of the training must be given by a person"

-- ---- paragraph 10: Supplementary provision with respect to a sufficient period of professional experience ----

-- src:20509 | 10 (1) Periods of theoretical instruction in the fields of finance, law and accountancy may be deducted from the required period of professional experience, provided the instruction—
-- src:20510 | (a) lasted at least one year, and
-- src:20511 | (b) is attested by an examination recognised by the Secretary of State for the purposes of this paragraph;
-- src:20512 | but the period of professional experience may not be so reduced by more than four years.
@ref sch 11 para 10(1) Theoretical instruction may be deducted from the required professional experience, by not more than four years (src:20509-20512)
GIVEN `the years of theoretical instruction in the fields of finance, law and accountancy` IS A NUMBER
      `the instruction lasted at least one year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instruction is attested by an examination recognised by the Secretary of State for the purposes of this paragraph` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`sch 11 para 10(1) the years of professional experience required after the deduction` MEANS
    IF `the instruction lasted at least one year` AND `the instruction is attested by an examination recognised by the Secretary of State for the purposes of this paragraph`
    THEN 7 MINUS (IF `the years of theoretical instruction in the fields of finance, law and accountancy` GREATER THAN 4 THEN 4 ELSE `the years of theoretical instruction in the fields of finance, law and accountancy`)
    ELSE 7 -- no deduction: "provided the instruction lasted at least one year and is attested by an examination"

-- src:20513 | (2) The period of professional experience together with the practical training required in the case of persons satisfying the requirement in paragraph 7 by virtue of having a sufficient period of professional experience must not be shorter than the course of theoretical instruction referred to in that paragraph and the practical training required in the case of persons satisfying the requirement of that paragraph by virtue of having completed such a course.
@ref sch 11 para 10(2) The experience route must not be shorter than the course route (src:20513-20513)
GIVEN `the years of professional experience of persons satisfying paragraph 7 by experience` IS A NUMBER
      `the years of practical training required of those persons` IS A NUMBER
      `the years of the course of theoretical instruction referred to in paragraph 7` IS A NUMBER
      `the years of practical training required of persons satisfying paragraph 7 by completing a course` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 11 para 10(2) the experience route is not shorter than the course route` MEANS
    IF (`the years of professional experience of persons satisfying paragraph 7 by experience` PLUS `the years of practical training required of those persons`) AT LEAST (`the years of the course of theoretical instruction referred to in paragraph 7` PLUS `the years of practical training required of persons satisfying paragraph 7 by completing a course`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not be shorter than"

-- ---- paragraph 11: The body offering the qualification ----

-- src:20515 | 11 (1) The body offering the qualification must have—
-- src:20516 | (a) rules and arrangements adequate to ensure compliance with the requirements of paragraphs 6 to 10, and
-- src:20517 | (b) adequate arrangements for the effective monitoring of its continued compliance with those requirements.
@ref sch 11 para 11(1) The body offering the qualification: rules and monitoring arrangements (src:20515-20517)
GIVEN `the body has rules and arrangements adequate to ensure compliance with the requirements of paragraphs 6 to 10` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the body has adequate arrangements for the effective monitoring of its continued compliance with those requirements` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 11 para 11(1) the body meets the requirement` MEANS
    IF `the body has rules and arrangements adequate to ensure compliance with the requirements of paragraphs 6 to 10`
       AND `the body has adequate arrangements for the effective monitoring of its continued compliance with those requirements`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The body offering the qualification must have"

-- src:20518 | (2) The arrangements must include arrangements for monitoring—
-- src:20519 | (a) the standard of the body's examinations, and
-- src:20520 | (b) the adequacy of the practical training given by the persons approved by it for that purpose.
@ref sch 11 para 11(2) The arrangements for monitoring (src:20518-20520)
GIVEN `the arrangements include arrangements for monitoring the standard of the examinations of the body` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the arrangements include arrangements for monitoring the adequacy of the practical training given by the persons approved by the body for that purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 11 para 11(2) the arrangements meet the requirement` MEANS
    IF `the arrangements include arrangements for monitoring the standard of the examinations of the body`
       AND `the arrangements include arrangements for monitoring the adequacy of the practical training given by the persons approved by the body for that purpose`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The arrangements must include arrangements for monitoring"
